From c8030f7f8ea563a97bf01e010fae4a7a48c69f0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: XR Phase 10 <xr@xr.local>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 10:24:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ci): cross-platform and website-build fixes (PR #43
 review)

1. website/scripts/generate-marketplace.ts: replace Bun-only import.meta.dir
   with fileURLToPath(new URL('.', import.meta.url)) so the website CI
   (npx tsc) and Vercel (next build runs its own TS check) pass under Node.
   Root cause of the Website + Quality Gate + Vercel failures.

2. src/update/channels.ts: normalize path separators in the Homebrew
   detection. On Windows, node:path join() yields backslashes so a darwin
   Cellar path never matched -> detectChannel returned 'unknown'.
   Fixes channels-update.test.ts on Windows.

3. src/state/workspace-store.ts: legacy-path detection now also accepts '\'
   (Windows separators); keeps the file at its recorded size-gate waiver
   (zero net lines).

4. src/security/guard.ts: skip Windows drive paths (C:\... / C:/...) in the
   egress URL scan. They are filesystem paths, not URL schemes; without this
   a shell command with a Windows absolute path is falsely egress-blocked.

5. test/trust/canonical-shell-isolation.test.ts: marker command converts
   Windows paths to the Git Bash /c/... form the canonical shell (bash)
   understands, so the marker lands where node:fs can find it and the
   hardened-mode block is audited as shell.isolated_blocked.

Verified on Linux: full suite 2750 pass / 0 fail; website npm ci + tsc +
next build green; bun run website:marketplace:check green under Bun; size
gate green.
